+## Explicit precision profiles in 0.20.108a0
+
+`mdstats-mlff-campaign init` now accepts `--precision single|double|refine`; plain init is canonical `single`. The generated TOML exposes the complete precision schedule rather than hiding it behind a profile name. `refine` defaults to 80% FP32 then 20% FP64 training, with a 0.5 learning-rate scale at the refinement boundary, a three-FP64-epoch floor, and a 15,000-gradient-update reference floor. DATA8 resolves epoch/update boundaries after loader exposure and binds the resolved schedule into training-protocol identity. PREC1 is configuration/identity only: staged execution and canonical-single critical-FP32 activation remain fail-closed until PREC2/PREC3.
+
+## Guarded multi-fidelity checkpoint evaluation in 0.20.107a0
+
+The generated production evaluator now screens every saved epoch on deterministic nested target and true-replay subsets (10% -> 33% -> 100%), reuses prediction coverage between rounds, retains statistically ambiguous/replay-plausible candidates, and publishes only full-fidelity finalist records into checkpoint selection. A representative 30-checkpoint qualification matched exhaustive selection while purchasing about 10.9 full-checkpoint equivalents. Historical bounded and exhaustive strategies remain available explicitly.
 
